{
  "summary": "Waits for the active chain tip to be initialized before returning from `Init.makeMining` when `wait_loaded` is enabled. This prevents callers like `Mining.checkBlock` from invoking `TestBlockValidity` when no chain tip exists.",
  "problem": "During a first start with an empty datadir or when starting with `-reindex` or `-reindex-chainstate`, `Init.makeMining` returns as soon as the chainstate loads but before the genesis block connects. If `Mining.checkBlock` is executed during this startup window, it calls `TestBlockValidity()`, triggering an assertion failure because the active chain has no tip and crashing the node.",
  "evidence": [
    "\"A Mining.checkBlock call in this window reaches TestBlockValidity(), which asserts that the tip exists, and the node aborts.\" (PR description)",
    "\"The crash can be reproduced on master using the functional test included in this PR.\" (PR description)"
  ],
